{"name":"Camouflage","hex":"#3c3910","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"camouflage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A disguise or covering up.","The act of disguising."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hide or disguise something by covering it up or changing its appearance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camouflage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Camouflage","blocks":[{"text":"Camouflage is the use of any combination of materials, coloration, or illumination for concealment, either by making animals or objects hard to see, or by disguising them as something else. Examples include the leopard's spotted coat, the battledress of a modern soldier, and the leaf-mimic katydid's wings. A third approach, motion dazzle, confuses the observer with a conspicuous pattern, making the object visible but momentarily harder to locate. The majority of camouflage methods aim for crypsis, often through a general resemblance to the background, high contrast disruptive coloration, eliminating shadow, and countershading. In the open ocean, where there is no background, the principal methods of camouflage are transparency, silvering, and countershading, while the ability to produce light is among other things used for counter-illumination on the undersides of cephalopods such as squid. Some animals, such as chameleons and octopuses, are capable of actively changing their skin pattern and colours, whether for camouflage or for signalling. It is possible that some plants use camouflage to evade being eaten by herbivores."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Flower_flounder_in_Kona_may_2010.jpg/330px-Flower_flounder_in_Kona_may_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camouflage","wikidata":"Q196113"},{"title":"Camouflage (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Camouflage is a German synth-pop trio consisting of lead singer Marcus Meyn, Heiko Maile and Oliver Kreyssig. They achieved a Billboard Hot 100 hit with \"The Great Commandment\", which reached number 59 in early 1989, and spent three weeks at number 1 on the Dance Club Songs chart. They also had two minor dance hits in 1989."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/14-07-26_Amphi_Camouflage_03.jpg/330px-14-07-26_Amphi_Camouflage_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camouflage_(band)","wikidata":"Q694873"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Maskowanie.JPEG/500px-Maskowanie.JPEG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Maskowanie.JPEG/500px-Maskowanie.JPEG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A soldier applying camouflage face paint; both helmet and jacket are disruptively patterned.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaskowanie.JPEG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Octopus_cyaneain_Kona.jpg/500px-Octopus_cyaneain_Kona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Octopus_cyaneain_Kona.jpg/1280px-Octopus_cyaneain_Kona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Octopus_cyaneain_Kona.jpg/500px-Octopus_cyaneain_Kona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Octopuses like this Octopus cyanea can change colour (and shape) for camouflage","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOctopus_cyaneain_Kona.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Variable_Protective_Resemblance_in_Lepidopterous_Pupae.jpg/500px-Variable_Protective_Resemblance_in_Lepidopterous_Pupae.jpg?utm_source=